WEBVTT

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.220
Here you go, Master.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.080
And table 3 wants to add a Milan-style cutlet and seafood salad to their order.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.860
Table 3, got it.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.270
This is a pretty nice place.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.270
Isn't it?

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.260
Hey, now, we have customers.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.370
Go show them to a table.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.500
Sure, sure...

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.140
You're good with your hands.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.310
You'll make a fine bartender.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.780
You might be a little too young, though...

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:06.360
Thank you.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.470
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:37.200
...the instant I look away.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.340
I just kept counting...

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.780
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:55.150
...that I'd vomited up.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:02:01.090
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:06.200
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:12.060
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.110
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:24.780
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:32.610
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.660
Any luck?

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.060
Not yet.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.180
What?

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.750
A response. Looks like the automatic identification system found a target.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:46.990
This guy?

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:56.060
Height, 174 centimeters. Weight, 59 kilograms.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.830
He's a match for the physical data that we were given, all right.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.170
Well, I'll be! Mr. Takano!

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.190
What a surprise to see you here!

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.850
Well, I was in the area, so...

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.560
I see you hired waitresses.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.930
They're just a couple of regulars.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.570
Looks like we're in for the long haul here...

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.250
Oh, you're back.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.150
Yeah...

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.630
You look like you spent the night here.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.590
No, I just got back from headquarters.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.640
The Administrator?

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:48.440
Is there something new going on?

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.440
I see...

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:03.720
I don't think it's worth reporting, but Yutaka Kobari never showed up last night.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.660
I see...

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:12.990
Good morning.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.970
Morning, Miss Karasuma.

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.630
That's a lot of food you've got there.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.980
We've got nothing to do...

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.720
Yeah...

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.790
The two of you look bored.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.570
Killing bugs.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:47.700
What's that mean?

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:53.610
Hey, Master... Is it okay for the place to be so empty?

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.410
Well, I don't know.

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.570
But considering that I manage to stay in business, wouldn't you say it's all right?

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:06.210
Still, this is a modern-day miracle...

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:08.960
That's not a compliment at all.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.190
Oh, welcome.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:37.070
Where did the Chief run off to?

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:42.990
Um, the Chief...

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.290
I heard you.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:49.760
Goodness, can't you wait until a body is done sipping his tea?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:54.840
What's your problem? If you heard me, you don't have to ignore me!

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.740
What was that?

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.000
No, nothing.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.080
So, the Chief...

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.210
You don't have to repeat yourself.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:07.080
The Chief is at Harry's right now.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.680
He is?

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:11.210
The two of them cause trouble when they're here,

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.220
...but we were the ones who sent them over.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.160
Since we are responsible for them, we can't let them run loose like this.

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.030
Oh, so that's why he looked so lively...

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.560
Did you say something?

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:28.430
No, nothing.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:34.580
Still, I hope he doesn't come back all worked up because he went to check up on them.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.700
Really.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.180
Oh, nothing.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:44.450
Geez, I get all worried and come over here, and what do I find?! Just like I expected!

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:49.150
You know, Mr. Kosaka, it's not as if these two are goofing off.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.990
We're having a bit of a lull here, so I let them take a break.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.760
In the first place, Dojima...

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:01.700
You're always at the office fashionably late, but over here, you show up bright and early!

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.540
What's THAT all about?!

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:08.540
Gosh, Chief, you look livelier than usual!

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.680
What are you implying?

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:13.640
Dojima.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:19.050
The Chief was just lonely because he didn't have anyone to vent his angries at.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:22.020
Robin, your Japanese really is strange.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.490
You think so?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.400
It's definitely strange.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.360
Really?

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:37.340
Yeah?

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.040
Around what time did the suspicious individual arrive last night?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:44.910
It was right after our regular check-in, so around 2130 hours.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:47.110
That all?

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.470
Yeah.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.160
Gather everyone in the briefing room.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:16.070
All right, this is the footage from last night.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.750
This is when the suspicious man enters the place.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.610
Look at the guy sitting at this table.

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:26.720
Just for a brief moment, he reacted to the man coming in.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:28.690
What does that mean?

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:33.150
You said that the man who came in had the same build as Yutaka Kobari.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.540
What? The two of you look like that means something.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.630
He reacted to a guy who looked just like Yutaka Kobari.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:47.610
There's someone other than us after Kobari?!

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.010
Check the footage from the past few days,

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:54.140
...and see whether this guy has been in Harry's before.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.510
Roger.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:20.900
Yutaka Kobari became the target of an STN-J Witch hunt two years ago.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:25.450
Our informant was the master of Harry's.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:30.080
Yutaka Kobari was betrayed by his own trusted father.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:37.290
And he escaped his STN-J pursuers and disappeared.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:42.230
It was about six months later that we received news of murders...

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.860
...in the U.S. that seemed to be his handiwork.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.840
Yutaka Kobari had made his way to America...

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.900
...and become an assassin for some criminal organization.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:55.540
However, there was a report from STN headquarters eight days ago...

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:59.170
...that Kobari had secretly reentered Japan.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:01.250
Mr. Amon!

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.680
He's been there before!

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.300
Master, what's wrong?

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.640
Oh, it's nothing.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:41.580
It's always the same. You call me out of the blue and ask me where I am.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:43.650
Sorry.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:46.960
That's unusual...

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.490
I haven't been sleeping much lately.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:53.830
It's a case...

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:58.370
A case that I had left behind two years ago has returned.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.640
I really shouldn't be able to think of anything else,

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:07.150
...but I keep finding myself thinking of you.

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:08.450
Strange...

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.310
Yeah.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:13.710
No, I'm saying that it's strange for you to be saying something like that.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.350
We shouldn't see each other anymore.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:25.590
I was wondering when you would say that.

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:33.380
Can I ask you one thing?

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.100
What?

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.070
Are you...

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.760
This is from the Master.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:32.100
He's on the move.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:37.700
Enlarge it.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.250
What, he's pulling out?

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:03.000
Dammit...

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.510
He's leaving early tonight.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:21.120
He just left.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:25.880
I know. As far as what we could see on this end, nothing happened.

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.160
Did he give up already today?

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:34.090
Maybe so. After all, it's been over a week.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.810
That's all right, Robin. Don't worry about that customer.

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.990
I'll wake him up later.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:06.620
Besides, it's late, so start cleaning up.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.660
Sure...

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.590
We're finally all alone...

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:38.750
Looks like you understood that message I sent.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:45.060
What's the matter? You haven't said a word.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:49.930
Or are you afraid of me?

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.500
Afraid?

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:55.910
You may be right. Maybe I am afraid.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:03.210
It's a sad thing to be a traitor.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.980
You have to be afraid, even of your own son...

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:18.790
Oh, welcome back.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:22.830
Karasuma and the others went home already?

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:26.030
Yeah, they've been stuck in here all day lately,

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.000
...so they wanted to go home early for a change.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:29.400
Early?

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:30.810
Yeah.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.410
That guy left Harry's rather early tonight.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:36.980
So...

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:42.850
Show me the footage from when he left the place.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:51.560
So, you really do hold a grudge against me?

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:53.000
A grudge?

00:17:55.140 --> 00:18:00.010
I guess so... It's true that I had a grudge against you.

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:05.750
When I left this country, I genuinely wanted to kill you.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:07.980
Do you know how it feels...

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:11.820
...to be treated like a monster and then thrown away?!

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.640
I'm a human being...

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.760
But just because I gained some strange powers...

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:37.200
Just because of that, you abandoned me.

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:39.540
That's right, for the longest time,

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:46.390
...I dreamed of coming back to Japan one day and giving you a taste of the terror I had felt.

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:53.330
But I was wrong.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:55.860
Yutaka!

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:05.230
You're going to call me by a human being's name?

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.680
You may not believe me,

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.940
...but I had always tried my best to think of you as an ordinary human.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:20.640
But once I realized that you and your power were too powerful for me to control,

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.420
...I just couldn't overlook it anymore.

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:26.390
Before you turned into someone who would harm others,

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:30.100
...I myself had to break the curse that flows within this body of mine.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:31.400
I knew that...

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:36.630
No, I realized that when I went to the United States.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:41.030
The only thing this power could ever become was a tool to kill...

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:45.580
Dammit, that wound from earlier is just now...

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:49.020
Yutaka, it's all right. Don't say anything more.

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:50.950
No, it's all right.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:56.490
I didn't expect to live much longer, anyway.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:01.120
The Mafia never lets traitors live...

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:02.830
Traitors?

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:06.700
Yeah, I betrayed the Mafia.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:12.300
I just had to see you one last time before the end...

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:19.250
Dad, I wanted to see you and apologize.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:20.580
Yutaka!

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:30.420
Dad... I'm sorry.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:03.930
That wasn't true. I didn't sell him out because I was afraid...

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:05.260
...that he would harm the people around him.

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:08.660
I was afraid of his powers...

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:12.430
Of the cursed fate that runs in my own blood.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:18.130
I don't deserve to call myself a father.

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:25.170
Miss Dojima sure is late.

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:28.650
Yesterday, she said that she was bored with doing this.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:30.580
So maybe she came away none the miser.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:33.540
I think you mean, "none the wiser."

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:38.220
Care for one?

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:43.360
Hey, Master?

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:44.730
What is it?

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:48.560
I always wanted to ask about your son.

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:57.550
You mean, what I thought about Yutaka?

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:01.240
I'm not sure.

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:06.550
Perhaps two years is longer than it seems.

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:09.720
Those feelings from back then...

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:13.920
Well, there is one thing I can say for certain.

00:22:14.860 --> 00:22:17.800
And that is that Yutaka really was my son.

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:21.630
"Was"?

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:44.780
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:47.640
Tell me.

00:22:48.850 --> 00:22:59.630
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:09.520
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:14.010
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:19.380
...all those promises...

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:25.780
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:31.580
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.780 --> 00:23:40.360
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
